Z||000000||Homicidal||07-04-2000||12:38 AM||||With my stereo!  My god, it just sounds SO good!  I thought about adding another 10" sub, but now I see it would have been WAY too much.<P>I have this band called The Anniversary, and their album sounds SO GOOD.  I equalized it perfectly!  <P>The bass lines hit just like it was at a concert.   Except the highs aren't so ear-piercing and the voices are just right so they aren't drowned out by the highs or lows.<P>It's just so much more fun to listen to music in my car than other places!  I LOVE the speakers in the headrest.  They sound GREAT.  I know once they go, it'll be damn near impossible to replace, but they sound so nice!<P>I heard a Fiero with the speakers in the sail-panels, I hated it.  The headrest speakers make you feel really "in the music."<P>It's funny, I have thin seat covers so I covered the speaker holes.  When people get in the car for the first time, I always get the question, "Man, where the hell are your speakers?"<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||7
Z||000001||webbee||07-04-2000||05:00 PM||||You can replace the speakers. The seat fabric has to be removed. There's a thread on it but I couldn't find it when I just looked, so it may be on somebodys web site. You peel them up like taking a wet t-shirt off. I've never taken the covers off a Fiero so don't know how hard that is. I have rebuilt seats on VW's and RX7's and it's a good afternoon per seat. I want to put leather covers on mine so will get there eventually. The speaks are an odd size as I recall, but there is a replacement. So not to worry!||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||07-04-2000||06:52 PM||||Headrest speakers sound like a$$ dude....||||reg||1
Z||000003||webbee||07-04-2000||07:19 PM||||Well I guess one man's ears is another man"s ass.<P>That's why I'm interested in a 6x9 in the dash. Them little headrest speks are unique and if you just use them for a bit of fill with something in the front they're cool.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Homicidal||07-05-2000||03:25 AM||||So true!  I'm sorry you feel that way GT Bastard!  I know every single person who rides in my car says it's the best or one of the best stock stereos they have heard!<P>Besides, they WILL sound like @ss if you turned off the 4X10's and my sub and just put them on.  They only are meant to handle midrange and tweeter, which I think they do very well!<P>I think coupled with the 4X10's and my sub, I don't have to nor do I want to blast my music to get a deep, rich sound out of it, so they sound wonderful!  <P>Either way, I LOVE my stereo!  Like I said, they make me feel like I am "in" the music, the sail speakers are too far and you can hear the dash speakers too much.  If you don't have good dash speakers, it sounds $hitty.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||webbee||07-05-2000||02:56 PM||||Found the thread on seat cover removal:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.mrmikes.com/faq.htm#getspeakers" TARGET=_blank>http://www.mrmikes.com/faq.htm#getspeakers</A> <P>Thanks & a tip of the hat to spyder.<P>Still haven't found the speaker replacement tip. I'll post it if I find it. Anybody else?<p>[This message has been edited by webbee (edited 07-05-2000).]||||reg||7
